  "Gillie Groats": {
    "Hello, I'm Gillie the Milkmaid. What can I do for you?": 567,
    "Absolutely! The secret is happiness.": 567,
    "The cows make the best milk when they're happy, and to be honest, they make too much!": 568,
    "I'm always glad that adventurers come by and help with milking them. I wouldn't be able to keep up otherwise.": 568,
    "Come to think of it, I'm sure my father keeps a few tricks up his sleeve. Why don't you go and ask him?": 589,
    "It would be! I'm sure he'll be happy to share some information with you.": 568,
    "Hiya, did you need something else from me?": 554,
    "The Duke is a good man, directing you to me! I've been running the milk side of our farm for a while now.": 569,
    "Were you thinking of being a competitor to us then?": 554,
    "You want me to drink a vial of mysterious liquid?": 554,
    "No, I think you should drink it, I'll know the quality of it from your reaction.": 593,
    "It is just milk after all.": 592,
    "It definitely won't hurt your chances.": 567,
    "That looked like a horrible experience.": 610,
    "Where did you even get that milk?": 554,
    "Cassius... I don't recognise the name. He's not mentioned anything about its source?": 555,
    "With how bad it looks, you wouldn't be any competition to us.": 589,
    "However, I wonder if I'd be doing a public service by protecting anyone else from it.": 555,
    "Now that you mention it, I've had an incredibly aggressive bull disrupting my herd lately. I've got him caught in the pen over there.": 590,
    "Perhaps you'd be interested in dealing with him? I'd owe you a fairly large favour.": 555,
    "Absolutely.": 588,
    "You succeeded! I'll let the Duke know that you're all good to start a milk business.": 568,
    "Oh? What happened in that field?": 554,
    "That bull was one of the business partners?": 554,
    "I wonder if his aggression is why Cassius' herd are producing such bad milk...": 555,
    "You think he's been stealing milk?": 554,
    "Why don't you go and talk to him about it! He may appreciate knowing the Brutus was bad for business.": 568,
    "Oh, just the person I wanted to see! I have something for you.": 568,
    "This is for helping out with that bull. Our cows are much happier these days.": 568,
    "One of our local milk enjoyers gave us some enchanted cow bells.": 568,
    "They seem to be quite versatile, enjoy!": 588,
    "I also have this for you!": 567
  },
  "Duke Horacio": {
    "Greetings. Welcome to my castle.": 588,
    "Oh wonderful! What sort of business are you looking to start?": 555,
    "Milk? Well, the Groats family still have their permit, and I can't start stepping on their toes.": 555,
    "I really couldn't possibly give you a permit without their approval. This is really their territory.": 589,
    "Why not speak to Gillie Groats? She seems to handle the milk side of the business now. Maybe she'll get you set up under their permit.": 556,
    "No, no. It's really quite important you speak to Gillie about this.": 589,
    "Don't go digging too deeply into that. Even I have some... commitments that I have to keep to.": 593,
    "Well absolutely, but I'm sure you'll find they're more than reasonable about things.": 593,
    "Entirely. Completely reasonable.": 610
  },
  "Professor Oddenstein": {
    "Ah, an interesting question! I believe it should create a rift in the very fabric of space! Opening a portal to some, hitherto undiscovered plane that exists parallel to our own.": 570,
    "It's a teleport machine.": 567,
    "No, I'm just one of the tenants. It belongs to the count who lives in the basement.": 589
  },
  "Cassius": {
    "You!": 567,
    "Yes you!": 567,
    "That depends. Do you like making money?": 554,
    "And do you enjoy... milk?": 554,
    "Milk.": 588,
    "Would you like to think more about it?": 554,
    "Profit!": 567,
    "Ten to fifteen percent, performance depending.": 588,
    "Ah, my name is Cassius. I got carried away.": 592,
    "But, we're going to construct an empire.": 592,
    "Of milk.": 592,
    "So, the first step is going to involve you doing a little... research.": 589,
    "You're going to cross the River Lum, find Gillie and Seth Groats, and learn about animal husbandry.": 593,
    "Then... Then you're going to cross back to this side of the river, and tell me all about how they've made their animals so productive.": 594,
    "It's a perfect plan!": 567,
    "Hey, I'm the one supplying the high-quality milk here.": 588,
    "Not to mention, my associate Brutus is already embedded in the Groats operation to work a different angle. That will prove most lucrative.": 594,
    "So, how did you get on?": 554,
    "Happiness?! That can't be the only trick they use! Surely you found something else?": 615,
    "Hand it here, quickly!": 592,
    "Now, this is most curious.": 554,
    "The idea that a happy animal will do what you want is frankly absurd. What if they choose to not produce. Are you supposed to respect that?": 590,
    "However, the writings on the systems of taxation are fascinating. I couldn't imagine Seth was smart enough to put this together.": 594,
    "No, no. Not quite yet. First of all, you haven't tried our milk yet, have you?": 589,
    "Don't look so worried. Here, have a try.": 588,
    "So, what do you think? The milk is fantastic, isn't it?": 554,
    "We're going to change the lactic landscape! Before we do though, I have another task for you.": 568,
    "We need... a permit.": 588,
    "The permit is to sell milk, not to make milk!": 588,
    "From the Duke of Lumbridge! Where else? You need to bring him our milk and I'm sure he'll give us our permit without fuss.": 590,
    "Of course! Soon the whole of Lumbridge will be drinking my, I mean our milk!": 593,
    "Why? What's happened?": 554,
    "Dead?": 554,
    "How could this have happened?": 554,
    "You?!": 614,
    "Don't tell me you killed Brutus and ruined my- our, plan?": 615,
    "Ruining the milk? The unique flavour was what I was trying to sell!": 615,
    "You should leave. I can't even look at you.": 614
  },
  "Seth Groats": {
    "Well well, what can I do for you?": 554,
    "Lookin' to get into the business, eh?": 554,
    "Well, always happy to help another budding farmer out!": 567,
    "Would always recommend me Groats Principles as yer basics.": 589,
    "Aye. First one is that happy animals makes happy farmers.": 568,
    "Second of me principles is to never take more than you need. Greed'll stop you in your tracks.": 589,
    "The last principle: never let the taxman know yer earnings. Money should be spent on the animals!": 593,
    "A way or two.": 592,
    "Anyway, feel free to grab me book on the topic from the shelf over there.": 589
  },
  "Fred the Farmer": {
    "What are you doing on my land? You're not the one who keeps leaving all my gates open and letting out all my sheep, are you?": 616,
    "You're after a quest, you say? Actually, I could do with a bit of help.": 589,
    "My sheep are getting mighty woolly. I'd be much obliged if you could shear them. And while you're at it, spin the wool for me too.": 590,
    "Yes, that's it. Bring me 20 balls of wool. And I'm sure I could sort out some sort of payment. Of course, there's the small matter of The Thing.": 569,
    "Well now, no one has ever seen The Thing. That's why we call it The Thing, 'cos we don't know what it is.": 593,
    "Some say it's a black hearted shapeshifter, hungering for the souls of hard working decent folk like me. Others say it's just a sheep.": 598,
    "Well I don't have all day to stand around and gossip. Are you going to shear my sheep or what!": 615,
    "Have you been shearing my sheep without permission!?": 614,
    "It's rude to shave another person without permission - don't be coming at me with them shears!": 615,
    "I guess no real 'arm was done. Hand the balls over and we can put this whole thing behind us.": 589,
    "I guess I'd better pay you then.": 610
  },
  "Reldo": {
    "Hello, stranger.": 588,
    "My name is Reldo. I'm the palace librarian.": 588,
    "Well, truth be told, I would probably be here even if it wasn't where I worked. I very much like reading, not to mention sharing what I learn with all who are interested.": 591,
    "Hmm... I don't believe there are any here.": 588,
    "Let me think actually...": 575,
    "Ah, yes. I think I have something, if you're definitely interested?": 568,
    "Well, if you look around for book called The Shield of Arrav, you'll find a quest in there.": 589,
    "I'm not sure where the book is mind you... but I'm sure it's around here somewhere.": 576,
    "Hello there, [player name].": 588,
    "Then perhaps you now have your quest?": 554,
    "No, I don't. However, I hear Baraek, the fur trader in the market, has had connections with the Phoenix Gang.": 589,
    "There are rumours that they are based in the south west corner of the city. Charlie the Tramp might be able to tell you more. He knows that part of Varrock well.": 591,
    "Good luck.": 588
  },
  "Baraek": {
    "Shh, shh, shh! Not so loud! You don't want to get me in trouble, do you?": 615,
    "I may do... but I don't want to get into trouble for revealing their hideout. Of course, if I was, say 20 coins richer, I may happen to be more inclined to take that sort of risk...": 591,
    "Okay, to get to the gang hideout, head to the southern gates of the city and then head down the alleyway past the Blue Moon Inn.": 590,
    "Down there you'll find a building owned by the VTAM corporation. That's where you'll find the Phoenix Gang. Just be careful. They ain't the types to be messed about.": 591
  },
  "Charlie the Tramp": {
    "Spare some change, guv?": 610,
    "Funny you should mention that... Rumour has it that they have their headquarters right down this alleyway. Though if I were you, I'd be careful about messing with them...": 595,
    "You never know. You'll find a lady down there called Katrine. Speak to her. But whatever you do, don't upset her.": 590
  },
  "Katrine": {
    "It's a private business. Can I help you at all?": 588,
    "Who told you that?": 614,
    "Hmm... I suppose I can understand that. So, say we were the Black Arm Gang, what would you want with us?": 556,
    "How unusual... Okay, let's say we are who you believe we are. Do you think we'd be recruiting people who just waltz in here saying 'hello, I'd like to play'?": 577,
    "Watching local thugs and thieves in action, perhaps? How do I know I can just trust someone who's wandered in here.": 577,
    "I'm not so sure...": 588,
    "Thinking about it... I may have a solution actually. You may have heard of the Phoenix Gang. I hear they have a very nice weapons stash not too far from here.": 590,
    "We're fresh out of crossbows, but apparently they have plenty. If someone were to aquire a couple for us, it would be very much appreciated.": 590,
    "Let's just say there's a local merchant who is refusing to pay some very reasonable 'keep-your-life-pleasant' insurance rates.": 594,
    "Him? No. However, I hear that the local law might soon be finding a crossbow belonging to the Phoenix Gang in his home...": 594,
    "I also hear that a similar type of crossbow might soon be used in a murder on the other side of the city...": 593,
    "Now, are you going to keep asking questions, or are you going to go get those crossbows?": 593,
    "Great! Apparently the Phoenix Gang's weapons stash is somewhere to the east. Ask that tramp outside. I'm sure he'll know more.": 590,
    "Have you got those crossbows for me yet?": 554,
    "It seems you're more skilled than I originally gave you credit for. Well done. Consider yourself a member of the Black Arm Gang. I'd suggest you now go and familiarise yourself with the rest of the ganghouse.": 591
  },
  "Curator Haig Halen": {
    "Welcome to the museum of Varrock.": 588,
    "The Shield of Arrav? The Museum has been searching for that for years! The late King Roald II offered a generous reward for its return!": 573,
    "You've found the shield? Let's have a look!": 571,
    "This is incredible! But where's the other half?": 571,
    "That does sound plausible. We will have to hope that another adventurer can recover that half.": 555,
    "I'm afraid the reward is for the recovery of the full shield. However, what I'll do is write you out two half-certificates. If another adventurer returns the other shield half, I'll do the same for them.": 591,
    "The two of you can then swap one of the half-certificates to make a full one each. Take that to the King and he will grant you your reward.": 590
  },
  "King Roald": {
    "Yes, citizen. Do you need something?": 554,
    "My goodness! This is for the reward offered by my father many years ago! I never thought I would live to see the day when someone came forward to claim it!": 569,
    "Well, in that case, it's only right that you both be rewarded. I will grant half of the reward to you and half to your companion. That means 600 coins for you. Enjoy it! You've very much earned it!": 570
  }
